    "summary": "I fixed `cache/lru.py`, and both tests now pass.\n\n**Root cause:** The cache never recorded when an entry was used. `get` returned the value but left the key where it was, and `put` on an existing key left it in its original position too. Entries stayed in insertion order, so the cache evicted whatever was put in first, even an entry you had just read. That's why the hit rate was low.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`get`:** now moves the key to the most-recently-used end on a hit.\n- **`put`:** updating an existin",
